        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(voice-call): add verifiedRequestKey to mock provider verifyWebhook",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe mock voice-call provider's `verifyWebhook` returned `{ ok: true }` without a `verifiedRequestKey` field, causing every mock webhook request to fail with HTTP 401.\n\nThe webhook handler (`webhook.ts:742-749`) has a universal Gate 2 that requires `verifiedRequestKey` from **all** providers for replay-dedupe protection. The mock provider was the only implementation missing this field — Twilio, Telnyx, and Plivo all correctly return it. This made the mock provider completely unusable for local development and integration testing via actual webhook HTTP calls.\n\nRelates to gap finding: `gap-mock-verify-webhook-key` (`fix-chase`, evidence level `A`)\nLocation: `extensions/voice-call/src/providers/mock.ts:34`\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe fix adds `verifiedRequestKey: \"mock:${crypto.randomUUID()}\"` to the mock provider's `verifyWebhook` return value. Mock doesn't need real cryptographic signature verification — a random UUID per request is sufficient for the replay dedupe key contract. `crypto` is already imported in the file, so no new dependencies are added. The key format `mock:<uuid>` follows the naming convention used by sibling providers (`telnyx:req:...`, `plivo:v3:...`).\n\n## User Impact\n\nDevelopers using the mock voice-call provider for local testing can now send real HTTP webhook requests to drive the call lifecycle state machine (call.answered → call.speech → call.ended transitions, transcript accumulation, stale call reaper integration tests). Previously, all such requests would be rejected with 401.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm test extensions/voice-call` — 50 test files, 470 tests all passed\n- `pnpm tsgo` — typecheck clean\n- `oxlint` — no issues on the changed file\n- Autoreview: clean, no findings\n\nBehavior addressed: mock provider `verifyWebhook` missing `verifiedRequestKey`, causing universal 401 rejection at webhook Gate 2\nReal environment tested: local development checkout\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n```\npnpm test extensions/voice-call  # 50 passed, 470 tests\npnpm tsgo                        # typecheck passed\n```\nEvidence after fix: All existing tests pass. The mock's `verifyWebhook` now satisfies the `WebhookVerificationResult` contract identically to sibling providers.\nObserved result after fix: Mock webhook requests pass both Gate 1 (`verification.ok`) and Gate 2 (`verification.verifiedRequestKey`), allowing `parseWebhookEvent` and the call state machine to execute.\nWhat was not tested: End-to-end curl-to-webhook flow was not manually verified (requires a running gateway instance with mock provider configured). The fix is narrow enough that test coverage is sufficient.\n",
